@prefix sem: <https://semblance.dev/ns/core#> .
@prefix val: <https://semblance.dev/ns/validation#> .
@prefix c: <https://semblance.dev/ns/component#> .
@prefix l10n: <https://semblance.dev/ns/l10n#> .
@prefix sh: <http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#> .
@prefix owl: <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix rdf: <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .

# Validation layer. A field says which SHACL property shape its value must
# conform to (val:validates); the layer checks the field's c:value (or
# c:checked) against the shape's constraints and derives c:error with the
# shape's sh:message, which every field already renders (and the a11y layer
# turns into aria-invalid + an announced message). Errors appear once the
# field has a value; a required field without one is invalid but quiet.
#
# A button with val:requires (fields) is disabled while any of them is
# invalid. The layer runs before the components (stratum -10), so they render
# its conclusions like any other input. Supported: sh:minCount (required),
# sh:minLength, sh:maxLength, sh:pattern (+ sh:flags), sh:minInclusive,
# sh:maxInclusive, sh:datatype (xsd:integer / xsd:decimal), sh:in.
#
# A field that edits a property of another node (c:controls, c:property: a
# combobox, a tag input) is checked by the values that node has: sh:minCount
# (quietly), sh:maxCount (with the message, past it; and val:full at it, so the
# field adds no more). The text typed into one that creates values
# (c:allowsCustom) is a candidate value: it is checked against the value
# constraints, and val:invalidEntry (the message) keeps it from being committed. A field may
# validate against several shapes; the first violated one speaks.
#
# A dated field (one the localization layer gives a date pattern: a date field, a time field) over
# a date or time property (sh:datatype, else the property's rdfs:range) also has its typed text
# checked: it must read as a date or time in the locale's format, or the field says how to write
# one (c:InvalidDatePhrase, with the locale's pattern). Its values are checked against
# sh:minInclusive / sh:maxInclusive as ISO text, and against sh:lessThanOrEquals (a range's start
# shape names the end property); a shape speaks for the property its sh:path names.

<https://semblance.dev/ns/validation> a owl:Ontology ;
    rdfs:label "Semblance validation layer"@en .

val:Layer a sem:Layer ; rdfs:label "validation"@en .

val:validates a owl:ObjectProperty ; rdfs:range sh:PropertyShape ;
    rdfs:comment "The shape a field's value must conform to."@en .
val:requires a owl:ObjectProperty ; rdfs:range rdf:List ;
    rdfs:comment "On a button: the fields that must all be valid for it to be enabled."@en .
val:invalid a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:comment "Derived: the field's value violates its shape (or a required field is empty)."@en .
val:invalidEntry a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:comment "Derived: the text typed into a field that creates values breaks its shape's value constraints, so it cannot be committed. The value is the shape's sh:message."@en .
val:full a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:comment "Derived: the property a field edits holds as many values as its shape's sh:maxCount allows. The value is the shape's sh:message."@en .

val:Check a sem:Rendering ;
    sem:requires val:validates , val:requires , l10n:datePattern ;
    rdfs:comment "Checks fields against their shapes and gates buttons on them."@en ;
    sem:targets sem:Component ;
    sem:layer val:Layer ;
    sem:stratum -10 ;
    sem:inputOnly true ;
    sem:follows c:controls ;
    sem:functionOnly """The error is the shape's sh:message in the viewer's language, a projection setting SPARQL rules
cannot see. A field over another node's property hears that property change, which is only known
from the data (the function's watches). And a button reads its fields' val:invalid through an rdf:List (val:requires): SPARQL rules
are re-run only for changes one sem:follows hop away, so the button would not hear a field become valid.""" .
val:Check-fn a sem:Rule ;
    sem:implements val:Check ;
    sem:function "validation:check" .
